-- title:
--   Igusa irreducibility: characteristic-p fibres of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ and let $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ satisfy $\Gamma_1(M) \le \Gamma \le \Gamma_0(M)$, let $p$ be a prime not dividing $M$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by all quotients $f/g$ of $q$-expansion series attached to modular forms $f, g$ of some common weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$) admitting integral $q$-expansions, the denominator series being nonzero. Let $j \in F$ be nonzero with Laurent series equal to `jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image of $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type power series `jNum`. Finally let $K$ be any field of characteristic $p$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra structure. The conclusion is that the scheme-theoretic pullback of `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase` $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\,F\,j$ — the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ descended from the structure maps $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to$ `chartAlgFin`, `chartAlgInf` on the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras `chartAlg` $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\,F\,\{j\}$ and `chartAlg` $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\,F\,\{j^{-1}\}$ of $F$ along their common middle chart — along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to K$ is an integral scheme, i.e. irreducible and reduced.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$p$ case of Igusa's irreducibility theorem for the reduction of the Kroneckerian model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p \nmid M$, where $H$ is the image of $\Gamma$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Together with the characteristic-zero case it supplies the geometric-integrality part of the good-reduction statement for the two-chart integral model, and it is used in the analysis of the Deligne–Rapoport level structures on $X_H$, in particular for the fibrewise statements about the charts `chartAlgInf` and the associated sections.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_pullback_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_qExpFunctionFieldC_of_charP.lean

